{"name":"Birch","hex":"#3f3726","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Birch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A nickname of the surname Birchall."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Birch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Birch","blocks":[{"text":"A birch is a thin-leaved deciduous hardwood tree of the genus Betula, in the family Betulaceae, which also includes alders, hazels, and hornbeams. It is closely related to the beech-oak family Fagaceae. The genus Betula contains 30 to 60 known taxa of which 11 are on the IUCN 2011 Red List of Threatened Species. They are typically short-lived pioneer species and are widespread in the Northern Hemisphere, particularly in northern areas of temperate climates and in boreal climates. Birch wood is used for a wide range of purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Betula_pendula_001.jpg/330px-Betula_pendula_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birch"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Areal_bereza.png/500px-Areal_bereza.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Areal_bereza.png/500px-Areal_bereza.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAreal_bereza.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Birch_bark_front_rear.jpg/500px-Birch_bark_front_rear.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Birch_bark_front_rear.jpg/1280px-Birch_bark_front_rear.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Birch_bark_front_rear.jpg/500px-